; A line folded onto a line it crosses: each candidate folds over the part
; of --v on the side away from toward, and (--v toward .u) measures where
; that part lands. .u lies below the a–c diagonal and to
; the right of --v, so the diagonal lands the upper half of --v on the right
; half of --h, nearer .u than the left half the other diagonal lands it on
; (#58). The side of .d folds over and .d lands on .b.

paper square
mark (map .a onto .b) as --v
mark (map .a onto .d) as --h
.u = free on --ab from .b at 1/5
fold (map --v onto --h) (--v toward .u)

